.TH LCTL-LLOG-CANCEL 8 2026-09-05 Lustre "Lustre Configuration Utilities"
.SH NAME
lctl-llog-cancel, lctl-llog_cancel \- cancel a record in a Lustre log file
.SH SYNOPSIS
.SY "lctl llog cancel"
.B --log_idx
.I INDEX
.I LOGNAME
.SY "lctl llog_cancel"
.B --log_idx
.I INDEX
.I LOGNAME
.YS
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B lctl llog cancel
is used to cancel the configuration record given by
.I INDEX
from the
.I LOGNAME
configuration log, typically on the MGS. This is useful if a persistent
configuration record was set incorrectly or is no longer needed. Note
that cancelling a record does not "undo" any effect it had on currently
mounted clients, it only prevents the record from being seen in the future.
See
.BR lctl-llog-catlist (8)
for a list of configuration logs.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI --log_idx " INDEX"
The record
.I INDEX
number to cancel, as printed by
.B lctl llog print
for that log.
.SH EXAMPLES
To cancel record 15 from the
.B testfs-client
conf_param log:
.RS
.EX
.B # lctl llog cancel --log_idx=15 testfs-client
.EE
.RE
.PP
To cancel record 22 from the
.B params
set_param log:
.RS
.EX
.B # lctl llog cancel --log_idx=22 params
.EE
.RE
.SH AVAILABILITY
.B lctl llog cancel
is a subcommand of
.BR lctl (8)
and is distributed as part of the
.BR lustre (7)
filesystem package since release 2.17.0
.\" Added in commit v2_16_53-8-gfe4b49635d
.PP
The
.B lctl llog_cancel
spelling has been available since release 0.10.0
.\" Added in commit 0.0.0-3210-gc5050e4125
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR lctl (8),
.BR lctl-llog-catlist (8),
.BR lctl-llog-info (8),
.BR lctl-llog-print (8),
.BR lctl-llog-remove (8)
